{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2136-08-25 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your hospital doctors. You were brought in tonight because your rehab facility said you weren’t taking your medications. Can you tell me your side of that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2136-08-25 22:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I wasn’t refusing them. They just weren’t giving them to me when I asked. I need my meds, especially the ones for my liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2136-08-25 22:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Well, we’re going to make sure you get all your medications here. You’ve had a complicated history—liver transplant, infections, breathing issues. We’ll go over everything tomorrow, but for now, we just need to keep you safe and stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2136-08-25 22:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s fine. I’m not feeling sick or anything. Just want to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2136-08-25 22:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work toward that. But first, we need to understand why things broke down at rehab. We’ll have social work and the transplant team involved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2136-08-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I reviewed your records. You’ve been through a lot—liver transplant for alcohol-related cirrhosis, a serious pseudomonas infection, and now this issue with medications. We did a chest X-ray this morning to check your PICC line. It’s in good position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2136-08-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The PICC line is for antibiotics, right? I was on meropenem before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2136-08-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but right now, the focus isn’t on antibiotics. Your urine test showed pseudomonas again, but since you’re not sick, we’re not restarting IV antibiotics. The bigger issues are your nutrition, kidney function, and making sure you take your transplant meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2136-08-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I eat fine. I drink the Carnation shakes they give me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2136-08-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re tracking your calories, and they’ve been inconsistent. You’re underweight—your BMI is below 19. That’s a concern after a transplant. We want you to drink at least two shakes a day and eat solid meals when you can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2136-08-26 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lab results show your potassium went up to 6.2 yesterday. That’s high and can affect your heart. We’re increasing your fludrocortisone to help bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2136-08-26 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2136-08-26 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be if it stays high. We’re treating it, and your levels are already coming down. We’ll keep an eye on it. Also, try to avoid high-potassium foods—bananas, oranges, potatoes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2136-08-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function dipped a bit—creatinine went from 1.7 to 2.2. But with extra fluids, it’s improving. This is common in patients like you, especially with dehydration or meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2136-08-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean my liver or transplant is failing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2136-08-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your liver labs are stable. This is kidney-related. We’re adjusting your fludrocortisone and monitoring closely. Your tacrolimus level is good at 7.6, so your anti-rejection med is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2136-08-28 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The psychiatry team met with you yesterday. They don’t think you’re depressed, but they suggested a low dose of citalopram for irritability. Would you be willing to try it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2136-08-28 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m not depressed. But if it helps me stay calm, I’ll take it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2136-08-28 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll start 10 mg daily. It may help you engage more with physical therapy and the team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2136-08-29 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been doing better with therapy. You walked 100 feet yesterday with your walker. That’s progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2136-08-29 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s tiring, but I’m trying. I just want to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2136-08-29 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re working on that. But you need to show you can manage your meds and care at home. Social work is helping set up home support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2136-08-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your potassium is down to 4.2, and creatinine is 1.8. That’s much better. We’re keeping you on the higher fludrocortisone dose for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2136-08-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m getting closer to going home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2136-08-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re aiming for discharge in a few days. You’ll need home health nursing to help with meds and check-ins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2136-08-31 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had a good session with physical therapy today—150 feet with supervision. That meets the requirement for going home with support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2136-08-31 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve been taking my citalopram. I feel a bit calmer, I think."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2136-08-31 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. It’s helping you engage more, which is important for your recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2136-09-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge plan. You’ll go home with a nurse visiting a few times a week. You must take all your meds exactly as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2136-09-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I understand now how important they are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2136-09-02 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. No signs of infection. The pseudomonas in your urine isn’t causing symptoms, so we’re not treating it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2136-09-02 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Shouldn’t I be on antibiotics just in case?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2136-09-02 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Unnecessary antibiotics can cause resistance or side effects. We’ll monitor and act if you develop fever, pain, or other symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2136-09-03 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling your follow-up labs. You’ll need weekly blood tests—CBC, kidney and liver panels, and tacrolimus levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2136-09-03 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Where do I go for those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2136-09-03 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A lab near your home will be set up. The transplant office will coordinate it. Call them if you miss a test or feel unwell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2136-09-04 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your nutrition has improved. You’ve been hitting your calorie goals more consistently. Keep drinking those shakes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2136-09-04 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I like the chocolate ones. Can I get more of those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2136-09-04 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can take them home. Two a day is the goal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discharge is set for tomorrow. You’re on a new med list. I’ll go over it with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll write it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take tacrolimus three times a day, mycophenolate twice a day, and the new citalopram—just half a tablet daily. Fludrocortisone is now two tablets daily for your potassium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the oxycodone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only as needed for pain, two every four hours. But don’t drive or operate machinery if you take it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. I don’t even have a car."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2136-09-05 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Also, no heavy lifting. And call the transplant office if you have fever, nausea, belly pain, or can’t take your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2136-09-06 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last day in the hospital. Your labs are stable. You’re cleared to go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2136-09-06 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. I’ve learned my lesson. I’ll take my meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2136-09-06 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad to hear that. Your health depends on it. The home nurse will help at first, but you need to be responsible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2136-09-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I eat normally? I miss real food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2136-09-06 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but keep it balanced. Avoid high-potassium foods. And keep using the shakes to boost calories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2136-09-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge team confirmed your home setup. Nurse visits three times a week, and your pharmacy will deliver meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2136-09-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2136-09-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We want you to succeed at home. Keep working on your strength and nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2136-09-07 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re being discharged today. Final check—your vitals are stable, labs are good, and you’re walking well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2136-09-07 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. I’ll follow all the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2136-09-07 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Remember: take every med as directed, no skipping. Weekly labs. Call the transplant office with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2136-09-07 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2136-09-07 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2136-09-07 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2136-09-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your med list one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2136-09-07 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll listen carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2136-09-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2136-09-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2136-09-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check-in. How are you feeling this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2136-09-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. A bit nervous about being home, but I’ll be okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2136-09-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. The nurse will be there tomorrow. Call us if anything worries you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2136-09-07 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have one question—can I have a beer now and then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2136-09-07 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No alcohol. Not after a liver transplant, especially with your history. It could damage your new liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2136-09-07 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I figured. Just wanted to make sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2136-09-07 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2136-09-07 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2136-09-07 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Transport is here. Ready to go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2136-09-07 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2136-09-07 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last reminder—call the transplant office if you develop fever, chills, or can’t keep your meds down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2136-09-07 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve got it memorized."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2136-09-07 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made real progress. Keep working on your strength and eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2136-09-07 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2136-09-07 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2136-09-07 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2136-09-07 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check—your discharge papers are ready, meds packed, and ride is waiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2136-09-07 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "All set. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2136-09-07 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve come a long way. Stay on track, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2136-09-07 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2136-09-07 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2136-08-25 22:26:00",
    "admission_end": "2136-09-07 18:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted due to medication non-compliance and social challenges following a complex medical history including liver transplant and recent infections. Over the 13-day stay, the focus was on improving adherence, addressing hyperkalemia with increased fludrocortisone, and supporting nutritional intake with calorie supplementation. Renal function showed mild, transient worsening that resolved with hydration. Psychiatry evaluated for depression and initiated low-dose citalopram for irritability, which the patient accepted. He improved in cooperation with physical therapy, achieving ambulation of 150 feet with supervision. Discharge was to home with home health support, a revised medication regimen including citalopram and higher-dose fludrocortisone, and instructions for weekly lab monitoring and transplant follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Adult failure to thrive",
      "Liver replaced by transplant",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Body Mass Index less than 19, adult",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of rectum, rectosigmoid junction, and anus",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Unspecified disorder of kidney and ureter"
    ]
  }
}
